<h2>Project Breakdown</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>The Mission:</b> Make a “Challenge Tomb”-level recreating the player experience in the Tomb Raider Survivor Trilogy based on an analysis of the games</li>
    <li><b>The Genre:</b> Action Adventure</li>
    <li><b>Character, Camera, Controls:</b> Single Player, 3rd Person, Keyboard + Mouse or Gamepad</li>
    <li><b>Platform:</b> PC, Windows</li>
    <li><b>Tools:</b> Unreal Engine 5.7.1, Unreal Modeling & Landscaping Tools, Blueprints/ Visual Scripting </li>
    <li><b>Role:</b> Concept, Layout, Blockout, Scripting, Pacing, Lighting, Prop Placement</li>
    <li><b>Team Size:</b> 1</li>
  </ul>


<h2>Level Design and Creation Process</h2>
<!-- Image on right side -->
<div class="breakout flow flow-80 skills">
  <div class="two-column">
    <div class="two-column__one flow prose">
      <h3>Analyzing the Challenge Tombs</h3>
      <p>Obviously, I chose to make a “Challenge Tomb” of my own because I loved to play the Challenge Tombs in the Survivor Trilogy. But to to reproduce the experience of the Tombs I first had to answer several questions: </p>
      <ul>
        <li>What makes these levels interesting and fun to play?</li>
        <li>What makes a “Challenge Tomb” a Challenge Tomb in terms of level design?</li>
        <li>Which incentives are given and which motivations are offered to players to play these side quests?</li>
        <li>Why are the Challenge Tombs rewarding to play? - Which rewards await players for completing the Tomb?</li>
        <li>Which kinds of challenges players have to overcome to complete these levels?</li>
        <li>How are the Challenge Tombs structured in terms of Pacing and Flow?</li>
        <li>What effect do side-quest-levels have on the general/ overall Pacing and Flow of the games?</li>
      </ul>
      <p>And finally the final and central question:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>How are Challenge Tombs as side-quest-levels integrated into the semi-open-world areas of the series and what is their function and purpose in otherwise linear Action-Adventures?</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The results of my study and detailed answers to these questions you can find here:</p>
